  "live_records": {
    "q-67513": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67513",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the equation for the common ratio $r$ of the geometric sequence whose $3$rd term is $4$ and whose $5$th term is $196.$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nApplying this formula with $n=5$ and $n=3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{3-1}={a}_{1}{r}^{2}, \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{5-1}={a}_{1}{r}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{3}=4$ and ${a}_{5}=196,$ we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{r}^{2}=4 \\\\ {a}_{1}{r}^{4}=196\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by dividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{1}{r}^{4}}{{a}_{1}{r}^{2}} & =\\frac{196}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{\\,{a}_{1}\\,}{r}^{4}}{\\cancel{\\,{a}_{1}\\,}{r}^{2}} & =\\frac{196}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{r}^{4}}{{r}^{2}} & =49 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
