    "q-64032": {
      "dom_id": "step-q64032",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the common ratio of the geometric sequence whose second term is $48$ and whose fifth term is $6.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{5}=6$ and ${a}_{2}=48.$ Substituting $n=5$ and $m=2$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{5-2} & =\\frac{{a}_{5}}{{a}_{2}} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{6}{48} \\\\ {r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by solving the equation for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ {r}^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-64032-a",
