    "q-250943": {
      "dom_id": "step-q250943",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the common ratio $r$ of the geometric sequence whose tenth term is $-8$ and whose twelfth term is $-72.$ You're given that the common ratio is negative.\n\n$r=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To find the common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence given two terms ${a}_{m}$ and ${a}_{n},$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're given ${a}_{12}=-72$ and ${a}_{10}=-8.$ Substituting $n=12$ and $m=10$ into the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{12-10} & =\\frac{{a}_{12}}{{a}_{10}} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{(-72)}{(-8)} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, solving the equation for $r$ and considering that $r$ is negative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =(-3)^{2} \\\\ r & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
